{#- A banner says a state of the APPLICATION the reader must not miss, on every
    page — offline, saves waiting, a maintenance coming, not production —,
    raised by the `banner` service into the layout. Never in a page's content,
    a block, a form, a row or a widget: what a page or a step says of itself is
    a message (message_warning(), the vue `message`). See usage/notifications. -#}
<div class="banner{% if type is defined and type %} banner--{{ type }}{% endif %}{% if compact is defined and compact %} banner--compact{% endif %}{% if class is defined and class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}">
    {% if message is defined and message %}
        <div class="banner--message">{{ message | trans }}</div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
